<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head><meta charset='utf-8'><title>FL2025_Exam 43</title>
<style>
body { font-family: Calibri, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; }
h1 { color: #C0392B; font-size: 20pt; }
h2 { color: #1F618D; font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 24px; }
.qtext { font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 8px; white-space: pre-wrap; }
.opt { margin: 4px 0 4px 20px; }
.correct { color: green; font-weight: bold; }
.selectedwrong { color: red; font-weight: bold; }
.selectedright { color: green; font-weight: bold; }
.explain { background: #F4F6F6; padding: 8px; margin-top: 8px; font-style: italic; }
.video { margin-top:6px; }
img { max-width: 500px; margin: 10px 0; display:block; }
</style></head><body><h1>FL2025_EXAM 43 - Ket qua &amp; giai thich</h1><p><b>Ho ten:</b> Hang Tran<br/><b>Ket qua:</b> 5/25<br/><b>Thoi gian lam bai:</b> 50 giây<br/><b>Nop bai:</b> 2026-08-03T08:02:14.372Z</p><hr/><h2>Cau hoi 1</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following statements on the use of checklists in a formal review is CORRECT?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. As part of the review planning, the reviewers create the checklists needed for the review [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. As part of the issue communication, the reviewers fill in the checklists provided for the review</div><div class="opt ">c. As part of the review meeting, the reviewers create defect reports based on the checklists provided for the review</div><div class="opt correct">d. As part of the review initiation, the reviewers receive the checklists needed for the review [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.2 Review process, Cái nào đúng về việc sử dụng checklist cho review? planning- checklist đc chuẩn bị, initial meeting- checklist đc gửi cho reviewer, individual preparation- checklist đc sử dụng để kiểm tra và tìm lỗi, review meeting- kết quả trong checklist đc mang ra phân tích, Follow up- checklist đc sử dụng để tổng hợp báo cáo. Dựa vào đó để loại đáp án sai</div><h2>Cau hoi 2</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following options BEST describes the responsibilities arising from the agile Whole Team approach?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Testers are responsible for developing unit tests and pass them on to developers for execution. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Business representatives are tasked with selecting the tools that the development team should use.</div><div class="opt correct">c. Testers are expected to create test cases collaboratively with business representatives and the development team. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Developers are expected to test non-functional requirements (performance, usability, security, etc.)</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.5.2, refer 4.4 về User story. Whole team approach, cái nào mô tả đúng về trách nhiệm đc raise lên từ team Agile whole team? điểm chính của Whole team approach là ai cũng có đủ kỹ năng để làm mọi task nên tính collaborative trong team là quan trọng</div><h2>Cau hoi 3</h2><div class="qtext">How is the whole team approach present in the interactions between testers and business representatives?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Business representatives decide on test automation approaches [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Testers help business representatives to define test strategy</div><div class="opt ">c. Business representatives are not part of the whole team approach</div><div class="opt correct">d. Testers help business representatives to create suitable acceptance tests [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.5.2, refer 4.4 về User story. Whole team approach, cái nào mô tả đúng về trách nhiệm đc raise lên từ team Agile whole team? điểm chính của Whole team approach là ai cũng có đủ kỹ năng để làm mọi task nên tính collaborative trong team là quan trọng. Chọn đáp án có sự hợp tác của các thành viên trong dự án là phù hợp với Whole team approach</div><h2>Cau hoi 4</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following statements BEST describes the Shift-Left approach in software development life cycle (SDLC) testing?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Test activities start as early as possible in the SDLC and are conducted in parallel with development activities. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Test activities start as late as possible in the SDLC and are conducted after the development activities.</div><div class="opt ">c. Test activities start in the middle of the SDLC and are conducted in parallel with development activities.</div><div class="opt ">d. Test activities are distributed across multiple phases of the SDLC and conducted in each phase according to the maturity level of the product.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.1.5. Mô tả nào về shift left là đúng nhất. Thì các hoạt động test đc thực hiện càng sớm càng tốt nên chọn A là đúng. B sai vì "as late as", C sai vì "start in the middle", D sai vì "across multiple phases"</div><h2>Cau hoi 5</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is NOT an example of the shift left approach?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Reviewing the user requirements before they are formally accepted by the stakeholders [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Writing a component test before the corresponding code is written</div><div class="opt ">c. Executing a performance efficiency test for a component during component testing</div><div class="opt correct">d. Writing a test script before setting up the configuration management process [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.1.5 Ví dụ nào về shift left là ko đúng? Shift left là các hoạt động test đc thực hiện càng sớm càng tốt: A. Reivew sớm, B là test đc viêt trước khi code, C là performance đc test sớm, còn D là viết test script trước khi set up CM là sai ( hoạt động quản lý cấu hình phải làm trước tiên, nếu ko sẽ ko quản lý đc các test script)</div><h2>Cau hoi 6</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is a characteristic of good testing in any life cycle model?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. All document reviews involve the development team. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Some, but not all, development activities have corresponding test activities.</div><div class="opt correct">c. Each test level has test objectives specific to that level. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Analysis and design of tests begins as soon as development is complete.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.1 good testing, đọc thật kỹ sách thì C đúng với sách. A sai vì từ all, B sai vì "Some, but not all, development activities", D sai vì "as soon as development is complete."</div><h2>Cau hoi 7</h2><div class="qtext">What is the role of testing in CI/CD?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. To give information for a risk based decision about release [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. To ensure that changes are verified before being deployed to production, lowering the risk of bugs and other problems [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. To show that system will work after release</div><div class="opt ">d. To decide when the software is of sufficient quality to release</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.1.4. vai trò của test trong CI/CD? tìm cách loại câu sai. D sai vì theo 1.1 thì test chỉ cung cấp thông tin cho các bên ra quyết định chứ test ko thể quyết định cho Release đc, Loại C vì theo 1.3 test ko thể "show that system will work", loại A vì cái CI/ CD ko liên quan đến phương pháp Risk based</div><h2>Cau hoi 8</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following BEST distinguishes the terms "validation" and "verification"?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Validation is confirmation through the provision of objective evidence that the specified requirements have been met while verification through the provision of objective evidence that requirements for a specific intended use have been met [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Verification is confirmation through the provision of subjective evidence that the specified requirements have been met while validation through the provision of subjective evidence that the designs for a specific intended use have been met</div><div class="opt ">c. Validation is confirmation through the provision of subjective evidence that the specified requirements have been met while verification through the provision of subjective evidence that the designs for a specific intended use have been met</div><div class="opt correct">d. Verification is confirmation through the provision of objective evidence that the specified requirements have been met while validation through the provision of objective evidence that requirements for a specific intended use have been met [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 9</h2><div class="qtext">Which ONE of the following options BEST describes Behavior-Driven Development (BDD)?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Expresses the desired behavior of an application with test cases written in a simple form of natural language that is easy to understand by stakeholders—usually using the Given/When/Then format. Test cases are then automatically translated into executable tests. [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Defines test cases at a low level, close to the implementation, using unit test frameworks</div><div class="opt ">c. Is primarily focused on non-functional testing techniques to ensure system reliability and performance.</div><div class="opt ">d. Requires testing to be performed after development is completed to validate software functionality.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div><h2>Cau hoi 10</h2><div class="qtext">What is a Definition of Done?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Criteria that a software product must satisfy are met and ready to be accepted by stakeholders [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Criteria that system is available for testing</div><div class="opt ">c. Criteria that system is available for releasing</div><div class="opt ">d. Criteria that software testing is stop</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 5.1.3, Definition of Done là tiêu chí mà 1 deliverable item phải thỏa mãn và chấp nhận bởi stakeholder</div><h2>Cau hoi 11</h2><div class="qtext">You are running a security test with the objective of finding possible network bottlenecks in interfaces between components of a system. Which of the following statements describes this test?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A functional test during the integration test level [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. A non-functional test during the integration test level [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. A functional test during the component test level</div><div class="opt ">d. A non-functional test during the component test level</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.2 chú ý vào 2 keywords: security test, interfaces between components nên chọn B</div><h2>Cau hoi 12</h2><div class="qtext">Match the correct description from A to D: A. A set of test cases or test scripts to be executed in a particular test cycle. B. A sequence of instructions for the execution of a test. C. Contains the expected results. D. The documentation of a goal and the agenda of a test session. to its corresponding test resource (test work results) 1 to 4: 1. test suite. 2. test case. 3. test script. 4. test charter.</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. 1A, 2C, 3B, 4D [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. 1D, 2B, 3A, 4C</div><div class="opt ">c. 1A, 2C, 3D, 4B</div><div class="opt ">d. 1D, 2C, 3B, 4A</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Tra glossary các khái niệm và map đúng, nhớ ghi lại định nghĩa và học thuộc định nghĩa này</div><h2>Cau hoi 13</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following BEST distinguishes the terms "validation" and "verification"?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Validation is confirmation through the provision of objective evidence that the specified requirements have been met while verification through the provision of objective evidence that requirements for a specific intended use have been met [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Verification is confirmation through the provision of subjective evidence that the specified requirements have been met while validation through the provision of subjective evidence that the designs for a specific intended use have been met</div><div class="opt ">c. Validation is confirmation through the provision of subjective evidence that the specified requirements have been met while verification through the provision of subjective evidence that the designs for a specific intended use have been met</div><div class="opt correct">d. Verification is confirmation through the provision of objective evidence that the specified requirements have been met while validation through the provision of objective evidence that requirements for a specific intended use have been met [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.1.1 hoặc tra glossary. Verification là kiểm tra xem đúng với tài liệu, validation là kiểm tra xem đúng với nhu cầu sử dụng. Ngoài ra các bạn cần loại cái cụm từ subjective evidence ( bằng chứng chủ quan là ko đúng) Test là bằng chứng khách quan.</div><h2>Cau hoi 14</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following statements about performing exploratory testing with test charters is correct?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. In contrast to black-box testing, the expected result is documented after a defect is found and not as part of test design [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Test charters are a useful tool to be used for testing when a detailed specification for the system under test is available</div><div class="opt correct">c. The result of performing exploratory testing by using test charters is finding defects and specification defects [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Exploratory testing and black-box testing use the same metrics for measuring test coverage</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 4.3 Exploratory test, tìm cách loại các đáp án sai đi. A sai vì the expected result is documented là TC của black box, B sai ở Test charters are a useful tool, C sai ở use the same metrics (2 kỹ thuật khác hoàn toàn nhau)</div><h2>Cau hoi 15</h2><div class="qtext">What is the BEST techniques to validate the correctness of function ?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Error guessing [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Checklist based</div><div class="opt correct">c. Equivalence partitioning and Boundary Value analysis [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Decision testing</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.2 kỹ thuật nào để kiểm tra correctness of function, đây là đặc tính con của Functional là tính chính xác, đúng đắn, sử dụng các kỹ thuật black box test để kiểm tra</div><h2>Cau hoi 16</h2><div class="qtext">In exploratory testing, a test charter is typically used to:</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Create detailed, scripted test cases to follow throughout the testing process. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Define the scope, objectives, and approach for the test session, allowing the tester to explore freely and unscripted testing sessions. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Ensure that all hidden logic and internal workings of the system are fully understood and documented.</div><div class="opt ">d. Restrict the tester to follow a fixed, predefined set of test steps to ensure coverage of all possible test scenarios.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.3 test charter là 1 phần của phương pháp session based</div><h2>Cau hoi 17</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is a primary benefit of using Behavior-Driven Development (BDD) in terms of stakeholder collaboration?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Improved software performance [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Reduced number of tests</div><div class="opt correct">c. Promotes shared understanding between stakeholders [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Increased test execution speed</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.1.3 chú ý vào stakeholder collaboration ( hợp tác giữa các stakeholder) là để chia sẻ sự hiểu biết giữa các stakeholder</div><h2>Cau hoi 18</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following best describes the impact of poor defect management on software quality?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. It ensures all defects are immediately fixed, improving software quality. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Defects may go unaddressed or remain unresolved for longer periods, leading to delay to release. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. It reduces the number of defects found in the software.</div><div class="opt ">d. It results in quicker releases with fewer defects.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Câu hỏi: Ảnh hưởng của việc quản lý lỗi kém là gì? chỉ liên quan đến quản lý lỗi thôi nên loại A thì lại là quản lý lỗi tốt, loại C vì reduces the number of defects found ko liên quan đến quản lý lỗi, loại D vì mô tả đó là đang quản lý tốt. Chọn B thôi vì quản lý lỗi tồi thì lỗi ko đc sửa trong thời gian dài dẫn đến delay release</div><h2>Cau hoi 19</h2><div class="qtext">You are performing test coverage analysis on a software component, and the results show that 90% statement coverage has been achieved. Which of the following is the most accurate conclusion?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 90% statement coverage guarantees that all logical paths in the program have been executed. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. 90% statement coverage ensures that every line of code has been tested.</div><div class="opt correct">c. 90% statement coverage indicates that 90% of the code has been executed, but it does not guarantee that all logical conditions have been tested. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. 90% statement coverage guarantees that no errors will be found in the code.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.3 định nghĩa của statement coverage</div><h2>Cau hoi 20</h2><div class="qtext">What does it mean if a set of tests has achieved 90% statement coverage?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 9 out of 10 decision outcomes have been exercised by this set of tests. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. 9 out of 10 statements have been exercised by this set of tests. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. 9 out of 10 tests have been run on this set of software.</div><div class="opt ">d. 9 out of 10 requirements statements about the software are correct.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.2 định nghĩa của statement coverag</div><h2>Cau hoi 21</h2><div class="qtext">In a typical Continuous Integration (CI) pipeline, which of the following testing stages is typically executed first to ensure that individual components work correctly in isolation?</div><div class="opt selectedright">a. Unit Test [BAN DA CHON - DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">b. Integration Test</div><div class="opt ">c. System Test</div><div class="opt ">d. Acceptance Test</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.2 chú ý vào individual components work correctly in isolation</div><h2>Cau hoi 22</h2><div class="qtext">In a CI pipeline, which testing phase usually follows unit testing and ensures that different modules or components of the application work together as expected?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Unit Test [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Integration Test [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. System Test</div><div class="opt ">d. Acceptance Test</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 2.2. câu hỏi nói là cái level nào sau khi thực hiện UT và đảm bảo các components khác nhau làm việc cùng nhau như mong đợi</div><h2>Cau hoi 23</h2><div class="qtext">What is the primary purpose of exploratory testing?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. To execute pre-defined test cases without considering previous test results [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. To perform testing based on a test charter, learning about the system and identifying defects during test execution [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. To focus primarily on regression testing after a re-release of the software</div><div class="opt ">d. To automate test cases to ensure that each feature is covered in every release</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.3. áp dụng chiến thuật loại trừ.A sai ở execute pre-defined test cases, C sai ở focus primarily on regression testing, D sai ở To automate test cases</div><h2>Cau hoi 24</h2><div class="qtext">What new concepts in CTFL v4.01 help tester evolve to the model that emphasizes flexibility, automation, and continuous feedback?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. A tester creates traditional test cases with rigid planning, ensuring that all test activities are carried out as planned in a waterfall-like process. They then use a control chart to track the defect detection rate over time. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. A tester adapts the test strategy dynamically by using adaptive testing methods, allowing adjustments based on feedback from early development cycles and continuously improving the test coverage. They use a control chart to monitor test progress and adjust their approach based on trends in the defect detection rate. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. A tester follows a rigid planning approach, ensuring that all test cases are executed in sequence without considering evolving requirements, using control charts to identify potential defects without changing the strategy.</div><div class="opt ">d. A tester sticks to the traditional approach of creating fixed test cases with minimal changes, relying heavily on rigid planning and rarely adapting the test approach, even in an Agile environment.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Câu này loại đáp án sai thôi, A, C, D sai ở rigid planning (kế hoạch cứng nhắc) ko phù hợp với từ flexibility,</div><h2>Cau hoi 25</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following aligns best with the new concept of “shift-left” in testing?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Test execution is scheduled strictly after all development is completed. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. Test activities (including static techniques) are moved earlier in the SDLC to catch defects early. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. Tests are entirely automated using old waterfall-based test suites.</div><div class="opt ">d. Testing is outsourced to third parties after system release.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 2.1.5 định nghĩa của shift-left là các hoạt động test đc thực hiện sớm</div></body></html>